# Shared-mailbox discovery dictionary.
#
# Dovecot needs to know which shared mailboxes to LIST for a given user
# before it will look at any ACL file. That lookup is `acl_shared_dict`
# (plugin block in local.conf), and this is its backing store.
#
# It reads a VIEW over shared_mailbox_members rather than a table of its own,
# so there is nothing to synchronise: add a member in the dashboard and the
# folder is listed on their next connection, remove them and it disappears.
# The rights themselves cannot work this way -- Dovecot's only ACL backend is
# vfile, plain files in the Maildir -- which is what
# shared-mailbox-acl-sync.py is for.
#
# ${DB_*} are substituted by scripts/entrypoint.sh at container start, the
# same way dovecot-sql.conf.ext is. The file is left unreadable by other
# users afterwards because this line contains the database password.
connect = host=${DB_HOST} port=${DB_PORT} dbname=${DB_NAME} user=${DB_USER} password=${DB_PASSWORD}

# $to is the member doing the looking, $from is the shared address being
# looked at; Dovecot builds this exact key when listing the shared namespace.
#
# value_field has to name a real column, and the value is never used for
# anything -- the view returns a constant '1' for it.
map {
  pattern = shared/shared-boxes/user/$to/$from
  table = dovecot_shared_mailbox_acl
  value_field = dummy

  fields {
    from_user = $from
    to_user = $to
  }
}

# Dovecot probes a second prefix when listing: mailboxes shared with EVERY
# user on the server. We do not support that, but leaving it unmapped logged
#   Error: sql dict iterate failed for shared/shared-boxes/anyone/:
#   Invalid/unmapped path
# on every single folder listing, which is how real errors get buried.
#
# dovecot_shared_mailbox_anyone is an empty view, deliberately -- pointing
# this at the real shares would list every shared mailbox in every
# organization to every mailbox on the server.
map {
  pattern = shared/shared-boxes/anyone/$from
  table = dovecot_shared_mailbox_anyone
  value_field = dummy

  fields {
    from_user = $from
  }
}
